      "event": "committed",
      "id": null,
      "node_id": "C_kwDOABII59oAKDA4ZDZkZTlkODBiNTE2ZTk0YjVmNTcxMzM2NzRjZTU1Y2IwMzQ5OGY",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/commits/08d6de9d80b516e94b5f57133674ce55cb03498f",
      "actor": null,
      "commit_id": null,
      "commit_url": null,
      "created_at": null,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/08d6de9d80b516e94b5f57133674ce55cb03498f",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "d5bdd50db2c475367c37d26a8ed4da0811154880",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/trees/d5bdd50db2c475367c37d26a8ed4da0811154880"
      },
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree d5bdd50db2c475367c37d26a8ed4da0811154880\nparent bfdcd9797cd1a1345bdaf7ee7ef48f94028262da\nauthor will <will@256k1.dev> 1782374358 +0100\ncommitter will <will@256k1.dev> 1790255117 +0100\n\nnet: reserve manual destinations before checking peers\n\nConcurrent -connect and -addnode attempts could pass connected-peer checks\nbefore either published a node. Reserve a normalized destination until the\ndial fails or its node enters m_nodes. Check connected peers while holding\nthe reservation, so proxied hostnames cannot use a stale precheck.\n\nKeep the reservation scoped to this call and leave the addnode scheduler\nunchanged. Numeric destinations include their port; unresolved hostnames\nuse the original string without an extra DNS lookup.\n",
